Measured (oplog 11:41): MOutArmZA jogged at 33 % (velHigh 26400) with acc / dec 80 = 1 % of Mot_Table 8000 (the jog family took the
runtime dAcc / dDec = the speed table's %, as golden SetSpeed does; the % reaches it since PARAMSYNC / golden Teach FormShow run
SetMotorSpeed). The stop reached the card in 30 ms, but the axis was STOPPING for 2.6 s and slid ~7700 counts after the release.

- WebMotorAccess.cpp Send1203SpeedValues (same lines): the JOG family's Acc / Dec = Mot_Table accDb / decDb (fallback: as before);
  the acc / dec ceilings also cover them; the PTP family keeps golden's values (auto flow unchanged). The axis's Mot_Table Dec is kept
  in g_jogStopDec; Stop1203 stops an axis this file jogged with that deceleration (kCmdAxStop value > 0), others as before.
- EtherCAT/Pci1203Control.cpp kCmdAxStop (same lines): value > 0 -> Acm_AxStopDecEx(ax, value) (vendor AdvMotApi.h; exported by
  ADVMOT.lib and the machine's SysWOW64\ADVMOT.dll, checked), value 0 -> Acm_AxStopDec as before (every engine / Galil / page stop
  leaves value 0).
- tests/test_web_motor_access.cpp test_jog_dec_100pct (end of file), 11:41 numbers through MotorAccessDispatch: jog Acc / Dec 8000
  (was 80), the release -> kCmdAxStop value 8000, an axis never jogged -> value 0. WebMotorAccess 1102/0; Pci1203Pure,
  Pci1203MotorRoute, EcatMotorRoute passed. Scan 0. wb_serve compiled; the link waits for EastSun's running program.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
